'''''The Traitors''''' (also known as '''''The Traitors UK''''') is a British reality television series broadcast on [[BBC One]], based on the Dutch series ''[[De Verraders]]''. It was first broadcast on 29 November 2022 and is hosted by [[Claudia Winkleman]].

Following the premise of ''De Verraders'', the show features a group of contestants participating in a [[social deduction game]] similar to [[Mafia (party game)|Mafia or Werewolf]], set in and among the grounds of [[Ardross, Highland|Ardross Castle]] in Scotland. During the game, a small group of contestants become the titular "Traitors," and must work together to eliminate the other contestants to win a grand prize, while the remaining contestants become "Faithful" and are tasked to discover and banish the Traitors by voting them out to win the grand prize.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Dubey |first=Shivani |date=11 November 2022 |title=Strictly's Claudia Winkleman to host BBC's psychological reality competition The Traitors |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a41938181/strictly-claudia-winkleman-bbc-the-traitors/ |access-date=8 December 2022 |website=[[Digital Spy]] |language=en-GB |archive-date=18 November 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221118030247/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a41938181/strictly-claudia-winkleman-bbc-the-traitors/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Duke |first=Simon |date=8 December 2022 |title=The Traitors remaining episodes dates confirmed by BBC |url=https://www.chroniclelive.co.uk/news/tv/when-the-traitors-on-bbc-25688883 |access-date=8 December 2022 |website=ChronicleLive |language=en |archive-date=7 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221207225657/https://www.chroniclelive.co.uk/news/tv/when-the-traitors-on-bbc-25688883 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |date=22 December 2022 |title=The Traitors: Why viewers became so loyal to the BBC reality series |language=en-GB |work=BBC News |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-63970819 |access-date=22 December 2022 |first1=Steven |last1=McIntosh |archive-date=22 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221222001204/https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-63970819 |url-status=live }}</ref>

Since the show launched, it has become a huge success for the [[BBC]], with viewing figures reaching 11 million by 2026. It has become one of the most watched British reality gameshows of all time. The show has gained a [[cult following]].<ref>{{cite web |last1=Dray |first1=Kayleigh |title=The Traitors isn't just addictive; it's a pop culture phenomenon. Here's why. |url=https://www.stylist.co.uk/entertainment/tv/the-traitors-season-3-cultural-impact/950298 |website=stylist.co.uk |publisher=Stylist magazine |access-date=29 January 2025 |archive-date=30 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251030074918/https://www.stylist.co.uk/entertainment/tv/the-traitors-season-3-cultural-impact/950298 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last1=Evans |first1=Greg |title=The Traitors finale viewing figures set new record |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/the-traitors-finale-viewing-figures-b2686779.html |website=The independent |date=27 January 2025 |access-date=29 January 2025 |archive-date=27 January 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250127121136/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/the-traitors-finale-viewing-figures-b2686779.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In 2025, a celebrity spin-off titled ''[[The Celebrity Traitors]]'' was created.

The British show also acts as a sister show to the [[The Traitors (American TV series)|American version]], with both being produced by [[Studio Lambert]] for the BBC and [[Peacock (streaming service)|Peacock]]. They share the same location, props, and missions, with the main difference being the hosts.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Bryan |first=Scott |date=January 12, 2023 |title='The Traitors' Was a Sensation in Britain. Can It Conquer the U.S.? |language=en-US |work=The New York Times |url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/01/12/arts/television/the-traitors-us-show.html |access-date=July 12, 2023 |issn=0362-4331}}</ref>

==Format==

Over twenty contestants arrive at a castle in the [[Scottish Highlands]] where they will spend their entire time for the duration of the game. On the arrival day, host Claudia Winkleman picks at least three contestants to be called "Traitors" and the rest are automatically called "Faithful". The television audience can see who have been chosen as Traitors, but the Faithful do not know their number or identity. Should the Faithful contestants eliminate all the Traitors, they will share the prize fund. If a Traitor makes it to the end, they receive the money.

Each night, the Traitors come together and decide upon one Faithful contestant to "murder" – and that person will leave the game immediately. The remaining Faithful contestants will not know who has been eliminated until the following day, when they do not arrive for breakfast. 

Each day, the group participates in missions to win money for the prize fund, which can reach up to £120,000 by the end of the game. During the missions, any contestant may separately win a shield that awards that player [[immunity (reality television)|immunity]] from being murdered, but not from being banished. In some cases, the contestant has the right or ability not to disclose if they won the shield, or to tell a restricted group.

Usually at the end of each day, the group will participate in the Banishment Ceremony – where the players gather at the Round Table to discuss who they wish to vote out before individually voting for a player to banish. Players cast their votes privately before [[Open ballot system|revealing their vote]] in turn to everyone. The person obtaining the [[plurality voting|most votes]] is banished from the game and must reveal their affiliation. In a tied vote, a run-off vote occurs between those tied with the highest vote tallies. If a second tie occurs, one player is chosen for banishment randomly among the tied players.

If during the game a Traitor is banished, the remaining Traitors may be given the option to "seduce" or recruit a Faithful to join them instead of murdering. Seduced Faithfuls may decline and can decide whether to tell the other Faithfuls of the attempted seduction. If only one Traitor remains, other than on the last episode, the Traitor instead delivers an ultimatum face-to-face with the recruit: if the player declines they are immediately murdered, and if they accept the pair can immediately murder another Faithful.<ref>{{Cite web |title=BBC One – The Traitors – The Traitors: How the Show Works |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/articles/2xRtJpWRbKcwPdXs7bZnxxH/the-traitors-how-the-show-works |access-date=12 December 2022 |website=BBC |language=en-GB |archive-date=12 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221212171149/https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/articles/2xRtJpWRbKcwPdXs7bZnxxH/the-traitors-how-the-show-works |url-status=live }}</ref>

===End Game===
After the final Round Table, the remaining players (typically four) gather at a fire and participate in the End Game. The group are given an opportunity to end the game by unanimous vote. Any vote to continue will lead to another immediate banishment vote. When a unanimous decision is reached to end the game — or when there are only two players left — the remaining players reveal whether they are Faithful or Traitors. If they are all Faithful contestants, they will share the prize fund, however, if any of these final players are Traitors then they will share the prize fund amongst themselves. To make their choice they hand Claudia one of two pouches: one marked "banish again" and another marked "end game". Each of the pouches is then thrown into a fire where "banish again" pouches cause the flames to turn red and "end game" pouches make them green. All active players see how each player voted.

For Series 3, in the final Round Table and for all subsequent banishments around the fire pit, banished players no longer reveal their true affiliation. In addition, the role of "Seer" was introduced,<ref>{{Cite web |date=24 January 2025 |title=What is the brand new 'Seer' power on the hit BBC show The Traitors? |url=https://www.yourlocalguardian.co.uk/news/national/uk-today/24884176.seer-new-power-bbc-traitors-explained/ |access-date=19 February 2025 |website=Your Local Guardian |language=en}}</ref> where a player, either Faithful or Traitor, can win the right in a task to meet in private with a player of their choosing who has to reveal their true identity to the Seer (the Seer's true identity is not revealed to the chosen player). Both players can tell the other players whatever they want about the contents of the meeting.  In Series 3, the Seer's meeting happened before the final Round Table.

==Production==
[[File:Ardross Castle - geograph.org.uk - 1234702.jpg|thumb|The series was filmed at Ardross Castle ''(pictured in 2003)'']]
The British show was commissioned by the BBC in October 2021 following the airing of the Dutch series earlier that year. The series was to be produced by [[Studio Lambert]] Scotland.<ref name="ATV 2021">{{cite news |author=Shaun Linden |url=https://www.atvtoday.co.uk/185126-bbc/ |title=Psychological adventure series 'The Traitors' for BBC One |work=ATV Today |date=5 October 2021 |access-date=22 December 2022 |archive-date=19 October 2021 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211019043839/https://www.atvtoday.co.uk/185126-bbc/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

The first series was recorded in May 2022,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Brett |first=Ivan |date=21 December 2022 |title=Ivan 🗡️ The Traitors on Twitter |url=https://twitter.com/ivanbrett/status/1605601059346403330 |access-date=21 December 2022 |website=Twitter |language=en}}</ref> and action took place at [[Ardross Castle, Highland|Ardross Castle]] in [[Ross-shire]], Scotland.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Metro |date=26 November 2022 |title=The Traitors: Where is the BBC One series filmed? All about Ardross Castle |url=https://metro.co.uk/2022/12/01/the-traitors-where-is-the-bbc-one-series-filmed-17863756/ |access-date=9 December 2022 |website=MetroUK |language=en |archive-date=9 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221209123726/https://metro.co.uk/2022/12/01/the-traitors-where-is-the-bbc-one-series-filmed-17863756/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

Presenter Claudia Winkleman was initially hesitant to host the programme but after watching the Dutch series became "obsessed" and jokingly said she "booked a train to Scotland".<ref>{{Cite web |title=Claudia Winkleman originally turned down The Traitors hosting role |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/claudia-winkleman-the-traitors-host-newsupdate/ |access-date=1 January 2023 |website=Radio Times |language=en |archive-date=1 January 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230101183631/https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/claudia-winkleman-the-traitors-host-newsupdate/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

Applicants had to submit a video application and go through several rounds of interviews, as well as a psychological assessment. Contestants were filmed constantly over a long day, finding out just before breakfast whether they had been 'murdered'. 'Murdered' contestants were driven away immediately and sent home, without being able to say any goodbyes. Contestants were assigned a welfare person to help with their well-being.<ref>{{Cite news|first=Dusty|last=Baxter-Wright|title='I was on The Traitors, and this is what it's actually like' - Alex Gray from season one reveals all|url=https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/entertainment/a46349516/the-traitors-filming-secrets-reality-alex-gray/|date=11 January 2024|access-date=12 January 2024|work=Cosmopolitan|language=en|archive-date=11 January 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240111193841/https://www.cosmopolitan.com/uk/entertainment/a46349516/the-traitors-filming-secrets-reality-alex-gray/|url-status=live}}</ref>

On 27 February 2023, the BBC announced that the show had been renewed for a second series, with Winkleman returning to host.<ref name="bbcrenew">{{Cite web |title=The BBC is 100% faithful to The Traitors as series two confirmed |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk//mediacentre/2023/the-traitors-series-two-confirmed-bbc/ |date=27 February 2023 |access-date=27 February 2023 |website=www.bbc.co.uk |language=en |archive-date=27 February 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230227110526/https://www.bbc.co.uk//mediacentre/2023/the-traitors-series-two-confirmed-bbc/ |url-status=live }}</ref> In May 2023, Studio Lambert revealed 40,000 people had applied to take part in the second series, in comparison with 1,500 who had applied for series one.<ref>{{Cite news |first=Isobel |last=Lewis |title=The Traitors producers tease series 2 tagline after 40,000 people apply |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/traitors-series-2-apply-date-b2340340.html |date=17 May 2023 |access-date=18 October 2023 |website=Independent.co.uk |language=en |archive-date=21 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231021123246/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/news/traitors-series-2-apply-date-b2340340.html |url-status=live }}</ref> On 1 September 2023, it was announced that filming had begun.<ref>{{Cite news |first=Megan |last=Nisbet |title=BBC The Traitors bosses warn 'the game is going to be different' in exciting series 2 update |url=https://www.walesonline.co.uk/lifestyle/tv/bbc-traitors-bosses-warn-the-27631896 |date=1 September 2023 |access-date=18 October 2023 |work=Wales Online |language=en |archive-date=21 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231021123246/https://www.walesonline.co.uk/lifestyle/tv/bbc-traitors-bosses-warn-the-27631896 |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 3 November 2023, it was revealed that a third series had been commissioned.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a45731101/the-traitors-season-3-renewed/|last=Stedman|access-date=11 January 2024|title=The Traitors renewed for season 3|work=Digital Spy|first=Emily|date=3 November 2023|archive-date=11 January 2024|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240111082459/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a45731101/the-traitors-season-3-renewed/|url-status=live}}</ref> In January 2024, it was announced that applications for Series 3 had begun, with almost 300,000 applications received.<ref>{{Cite web |title=How to apply for The Traitors: Registration details and application |url=https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/reality-tv/the-traitors-how-to-apply/ |access-date=29 January 2024 |website=Radio Times |language=en-GB |archive-date=29 January 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240129100941/https://www.radiotimes.com/tv/entertainment/reality-tv/the-traitors-how-to-apply/ |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web | url=https://deadline.com/2024/04/celebrity-the-traitors-bbc-2025-1235888093/ | title=Celebrity Version of 'The Traitors' Set to Launch Next Year on the BBC | date=18 April 2024 | access-date=12 May 2024 | archive-date=12 May 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240512171319/https://deadline.com/2024/04/celebrity-the-traitors-bbc-2025-1235888093/ | url-status=live }}</ref> The series was filming as of May 2024.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://deadline.com/2024/05/the-traitors-liz-truss-contestant-bbc-celebrity-series-1235912891/ | title='The Traitors' Producer Wants Former Prime Minister Liz Truss for BBC Celebrity Series | date=12 May 2024 | access-date=12 May 2024 | archive-date=12 May 2024 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240512171319/https://deadline.com/2024/05/the-traitors-liz-truss-contestant-bbc-celebrity-series-1235912891/ | url-status=live }}</ref>

In August 2024, ahead of the release of the third series, the BBC announced that the show had not only been renewed for a fourth series but a [[The Celebrity Traitors series 1|celebrity series]] will also be produced.<ref>{{Cite web |date=4 March 2025 |title=A celeb version of The Traitors is coming - here's what we know so far |url=https://www.goodhousekeeping.com/uk/lifestyle/a61955476/celebrity-the-traitors/ |access-date=7 March 2025 |website=Good Housekeeping |language=en-GB |archive-date=12 March 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250312133539/https://www.goodhousekeeping.com/uk/lifestyle/a61955476/celebrity-the-traitors/ |url-status=live }}</ref> Filming for both versions took place during 2025.<ref>{{cite web|title=Celebrity Series of The Traitors is coming to BBC One and BBC iPlayer with fourth series also confirmed from Studio Lambert|url=https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2024/the-traitors-celebrity-series-four-confirmed|publisher=BBC|accessdate=9 January 2025|archive-date=6 February 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250206234439/https://www.bbc.com/mediacentre/2024/the-traitors-celebrity-series-four-confirmed|url-status=live}}</ref> Applications for the fourth series opened on 22 August 2024 and closed on 9 February 2025.<ref>{{cite web|title=Applications are now open for The Traitors series 4|url=https://hellorayo.co.uk/hits-radio/entertainment/television/the-traitors-applications/|publisher=Rayo|accessdate=9 January 2025|archive-date=23 January 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250123093150/https://hellorayo.co.uk/hits-radio/entertainment/television/the-traitors-applications/|url-status=live}}</ref>

=== Atmosphere and music ===
To emphasize the show's authentic Scottish Highlands setting at Ardross Castle, production utilizes live traditional musicians to frame dramatic events, missions, and contestant arrivals. Among the local musicians featured on-screen is James Mackenzie, Dingwall, a veteran bagpiper from Ross and Cromarty who performs with the Alness Pipe Band. Known for his mastery of traditional pibroch (classical pipe music), James is dressed in traditional Highland attire—including the Mackenzie tartan—to provide the show's distinct, tense auditory backdrop.

In March 2026, [[BBC]] announced a three-year deal that will keep ''The Traitors'' and ''[[The Celebrity Traitors]]'' in production until 2030.<ref>{{cite web|title=BBC remains Faithful to The Traitors and The Celebrity Traitors until at least 2030|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/mediacentre/2026/bbc-remains-faithful-to-the-traitors-the-celebrity-traitors-2030/|publisher=[[BBC]]|accessdate=12 March 2026}}</ref>

