== Reception ==
=== Critical reception ===
The series was generally well received by critics, who praised the programme for being "fresh, yet familiar", likening it to party games such as [[Mafia (party game)|Mafia]] or [[wink murder]].<ref name=":0">{{Cite news |last=McIntosh |first=Steven |date=22 December 2022 |title=The Traitors: Why viewers became so loyal to the BBC reality series |language=en-GB |work=[[BBC News]] |url=https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-63970819 |access-date=22 December 2022 |archive-date=22 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221222001204/https://www.bbc.com/news/entertainment-arts-63970819 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{Cite news |last=Long |first=Camilla |date=4 December 2022 |title=The Traitors: I'm a TV critic, get me out of here |language=en |work=[[The Times]] |url=https://www.thetimes.com/culture/article/the-traitors-im-a-tv-critic-get-me-out-of-here-5c9bzs20x |url-access=subscription |access-date=22 December 2022 |issn=0140-0460 |archive-date=25 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251125034702/https://www.thetimes.com/culture/article/the-traitors-im-a-tv-critic-get-me-out-of-here-5c9bzs20x |url-status=live }}</ref> Rebecca Nicholson of ''The Guardian'' says the format "feels like a revival of the early, more innocent days of reality TV", calling it "''[[The White Lotus]]'' meets ''[[Big Brother (British TV series) series 1|Big Brother 1]]''".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nicholson |first=Rebecca |date=19 December 2022 |title=I'm 100% faithful: The Traitors is the most exquisite reality TV of the year |url=https://www.theguardian.com/tv-and-radio/2022/dec/19/the-traitors-bbc-most-exquisite-reality-tv |access-date=22 December 2022 |website=[[The Guardian]] |language=en}}</ref> ''[[The Tab]]'' believed that social media helped the success of the show: "The memes and everyone live-[[Twitter|tweeting]] it has played a big part in its success. Nobody wants to miss out on a reality TV show that everyone is talking about."<ref name=":0" /> Isobel Lewis of ''[[The Independent]]'' was more critical, however, saying it "definitely isn't a perfect reality show, or even the best in its genre right now, but it is pretty entertaining."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Lewis |first=Isobel |date=29 November 2022 |title=The Traitors might not be very Christmassy, but it sure is fun – review |url=https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/reviews/the-traitors-claudia-winkleman-bbc-b2235420.html |access-date=22 December 2022 |website=[[The Independent]] |language=en |archive-date=22 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221222143414/https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/tv/reviews/the-traitors-claudia-winkleman-bbc-b2235420.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

=== Viewership ===
The series saw an average audience of 5.4 million, with a peak of 6.2 million for the first episode. By the end of February 2023, ''The Traitors'' had been viewed over 34 million times on [[BBC iPlayer]].<ref name="bbcrenew" />

The BBC stated that ''The Traitors'' was the biggest new series for young audiences across all BBC content in 2022, with a 1.3 million average audience across the series and a peak of 1.5 million for the final.<ref name="bbcrenew" />

