To accompany the second series in January 2024, a follow-up television programme and [[BBC Sounds]] [[podcast]] was introduced, called ''The Traitors: Uncloaked'' produced by Listen. The first episode aired on 5 January 2024. It was hosted by [[Ed Gamble]] and broadcast on [[BBC Two]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.tvzoneuk.com/post/traitors-uncloaked-newsrep2 |title=Sleep with One Eye Open: Traitors US and Traitors UK Now Available on 10 Play |work=TV Zone |date=3 January 2024 |access-date=29 January 2024 |archive-date=10 February 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240210042935/https://www.tvzoneuk.com/post/traitors-uncloaked-newsrep2 |url-status=live}}</ref> The final episode of ''Uncloaked'' which aired on BBC Two directly after the final received 3.97 million viewers.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.barb.co.uk/viewing-data/four-screen-dashboard/|title=Four-screen dashboard (7-day data)|publisher=[[BARB]]|access-date=6 February 2024|archive-date=2 February 2019|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190202221734/https://www.barb.co.uk/viewing-data/four-screen-dashboard/|url-status=live}}</ref> ''Uncloaked'' returned with the same format to accompany the third series in 2025. For the fourth series in 2026, episodes from 2 January onwards the show were moved to BBC One.

==''The Traitors at the Proms''==
On 26 July 2025, Winkleman presented a [[BBC Proms]] concert at London's [[Royal Albert Hall]] with music from the [[BBC Scottish Symphony Orchestra]], [[BBC Symphony Chorus]] and the [[BBC Singers]] directed by Irish conductor Karen Ní Bhroin. Inspired by the show's tense and haunting soundtrack, the Prom features melodramatic versions of pop tunes heard in the series, from [[Britney Spears]]’s ''Toxic'' and [[Olivia Rodrigo]]’s ''Vampire'' to [[Billie Eilish]]’s ''Bad Guy'', all given a signature gothic, symphonic twist performed alongside guest vocalists [[Andrea Lykke Oehlenschlæger]], HAYLA and Darrell Smith.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/m002p19b|title=BBC Radio 3 - BBC Proms, 2025, The Traitors at the Proms|date=1 January 2026|website=BBC|accessdate=1 January 2026|archive-date=25 December 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251225002023/https://www.bbc.co.uk/programmes/m002p19b|url-status=live}}</ref> The matinee performance of the Prom was broadcast live on [[BBC Radio 3]] and repeated on [[BBC Radio 2]] on 24 August; highlights were later shown on 1 January 2026 on BBC One.

== Interactive merchandise ==
After the first series, the BBC published a ''Traitors'' card game and puzzle book. In September 2023, a [[board game]], called ''The Traitors'', was released.<ref>{{cite news |author=Kate Goodacre |url=https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a44999294/the-traitors-board-game-buy/ |title=The Traitors board game is finally available to buy |work=[[Digital Spy]] |date=September 2023 |access-date=21 October 2023 |archive-date=19 October 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231019115951/https://www.digitalspy.com/tv/reality-tv/a44999294/the-traitors-board-game-buy/ |url-status=live }}</ref>

For Series 2, a Traitors [[Mobile app|app]] was released, allowing users to predict what will happen in the series and gain points for correct predictions. It was described as "the perfect synchronicity between programme content and interactive platform".<ref>{{cite news|author=Keith Stuart |url=https://www.theguardian.com/games/2024/jan/10/pushing-buttons-the-traitors-tv-show-game |title=Pushing Buttons: Why the Traitors online game is a new frontier for the way we watch TV |work=The Guardian |date=10 January 2024 |access-date=12 January 2024}}</ref>

==International broadcast==
In Australia, the series was made available to stream on [[10 Play (Network 10)|10 Play]] in March 2023, as a companion to the [[The Traitors (Australian TV series)|Australian version]] aired by the network.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://10play.com.au/10-play-trending/articles/sleep-with-one-eye-open-traitors-us-and-traitors-uk-now-available-on-10-play/tpa230322bnyij | title=Uncloaked: Ed Gamble to host The Traitors spin-off on BBC Two | date=23 March 2023 |website=10play.com.au}}</ref> The celebrity edition aired fast-tracked on 10Play and also aired on linear television on [[Network 10]] on a 2-week delay.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://tvtonight.com.au/2025/10/airdate-the-celebrity-traitors-uk.html|title=Airdate: The Celebrity Traitors UK &#124; TV Tonight|date=17 October 2025|website=tvtonight.com.au}}</ref>

In the United States, the show is available to stream on [[Peacock (streaming service)|Peacock]], the broadcaster of the [[The Traitors (American TV series)|American version]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.c21media.net/news/uk-australian-versions-of-the-traitors-uncovered-by-peacock-for-us/ | title=UK, Australian versions of the Traitors uncovered by Peacock for US | website=c21media.net | access-date=19 March 2023 | archive-date=7 March 2023 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230307144421/https://www.c21media.net/news/uk-australian-versions-of-the-traitors-uncovered-by-peacock-for-us/ | url-status=live }}</ref>

In Canada, the show is available to stream on [[Crave (streaming service)|Crave]].<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.memorabletv.com/news/u-k-u-s-australian-versions-of-the-traitors-now-streaming-on-crave/ | title=U.K., U.S. & Australian Versions of 'The Traitors' Now Streaming on Crave | date=9 April 2023 | website=memorabletv.com | access-date=10 April 2023 | archive-date=10 April 2023 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230410034716/https://www.memorabletv.com/news/u-k-u-s-australian-versions-of-the-traitors-now-streaming-on-crave/ | url-status=live }}</ref> The [[The Traitors (Canadian TV series)|Canadian version]] of the series began on 2 October 2023 on [[CTV Television Network|CTV]].

In New Zealand, the show is available to stream on [[ThreeNow]], the same broadcaster as the New Zealand version.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://thespinoff.co.nz/pop-culture/04-09-2023/new-to-streaming-what-to-watch-on-netflix-nz-neon-and-more-this-week-15 | title=New to streaming: What to watch on Netflix NZ, Neon and more this week | date=4 September 2023 | access-date=4 September 2023 | archive-date=4 September 2023 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230904090252/https://thespinoff.co.nz/pop-culture/04-09-2023/new-to-streaming-what-to-watch-on-netflix-nz-neon-and-more-this-week-15 | url-status=live }}</ref>

In Sweden, the first series was made available with Swedish subtitles on TV4 Play not long after the premiere of ''Förrädarna'', TV4's own version. Many other countries have followed the same route.

In Poland in December 2024, the first series was broadcast on [[TVN 7]] in nighttime slot and each episode (after it had aired) was made available to watch on a streaming service [[Player.pl|Player]].

The Croatian network [[RTL (Croatian TV channel)|RTL]], which is set to broadcast the Croatian edition of the series, began releasing ''The Traitors UK'' on its streaming service [[Voyo]] on 1 January 2025.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.rtl.hr/emisije/traitors-uk|title=The Traitors UK {{!}} RTL|website=rtl.hr|publisher=[[RTL (Croatian TV channel)|RTL]]|access-date=6 January 2025|language=hr|archive-date=6 January 2025|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250106110229/https://www.rtl.hr/emisije/traitors-uk|url-status=live}}</ref>

In Ireland, the first series was added to the [[RTÉ Player]] in the beginning of July 2025 before the series began airing on [[RTÉ2]] ahead of [[The Traitors Ireland|RTÉ's own version of the show]] premiering in late August.

